    "chunk_text": "Abans Group marks inaugural Founder\u2019s Day\n\nThe Abans Group celebrated its first-ever Founder\u2019s Day in 2026, marking a significant milestone on the eve of the 90th birthday of its founder, Aban Pestonjee, the visionary behind a legacy spanning more than five decades.\n\nWhat began in 1968 in a closed economy, as a modest corner shop in Bambalapitiya has since evolved into one of Sri Lanka\u2019s leading diversified conglomerates. In its early days, Mrs. Pestonjee sourced a limited range of appliances from embassy auctions, offering customers not only products but also after-sales service with a guarantee, which was an uncommon practice at the time. This customer-first philosophy continues to define the Group\u2019s operations today.\n\nWhen Sri Lanka embraced the open economy in 1977, major English companies held the lion\u2019s share of brands. Yet, she persisted by consistently writing to to principals of major brands in demand at the time, until Electrolux responded to her request, visited the showroom and saw that she was offering after-sales services. This prompted the brand principal to sign on to become the first global brand available for sale under Abans. This was followed by other agencies, such as Belling, Hoover, Pyrex and Corning joining the Abans fray.\n\nOver the years, the Abans Group has expanded its footprint across multiple sectors, including household electronics, retail, real estate development, environmental management, IT services, automobiles, and logistics. At the heart of this growth are the enduring values instilled by its founder: Honesty, Hard work, and Perseverance. Today, the Group stands strong with over 10,000 employees, united by a culture of trust, loyalty, and shared purpose."
  },
