    "md5": "1848f70c99c99e31d9d6ac6decd7b95a",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1678,
    "chunk_text": "The MoU is expected to facilitate substantial investment inflows into key sectors including agriculture, tourism, imports and exports, real estate, as well as geology and mining. It is also anticipated to generate meaningful employment opportunities, contributing to Sri Lanka\u2019s broader economic growth and development.\n\nSpeaking on the partnership, Dr. Nalaka Silva noted that AHC Group continues to play a pivotal role in advancing Sri Lanka\u2019s agricultural landscape through innovative and sustainable initiatives.\n\nDr. Silva further extended an open invitation to the public to engage with AHC Group\u2019s investment opportunities, highlighting the company\u2019s focus on transparency, trust, and long-term value creation. He expressed confidence that the newly signed agreement with AACCI would unlock significant economic benefits for Sri Lanka, while also fostering stronger international business linkages.\n\nIn line with this vision, AHC Group and ICAPIFPO are preparing to host a major international workshop and conference in Sri Lanka this August. The event, organised by the Global India Business Forum (GIBF) in association with ICAPIFPO and AHC Group, is expected to attract global business leaders, industry experts, and professionals from over 25 countries. More than 25 ambassadors and high commissioners are also scheduled to attend, underscoring the event\u2019s international significance.\n\nDr. Silva emphasised that the upcoming conference will serve as a powerful platform to open new global opportunities for Sri Lankan entrepreneurs and businesses. Further details of the event are expected to be announced through official media channels in the near future."
