    "chunk_text": "SHEvolve \u201926: Empowering conversations, inspiring change\n\nSHEvolve \u201926, a pioneering women-empowerment initiative organized by AIESEC in University of Colombo, is set to take place on May 9th from 9.00 a.m. onwards at the New Arts Theatre, University of Colombo. Building on the success of its previous edition, which welcomed over 500 delegates alongside renowned guest Ms. Anudi Gunasekara, the Miss World Sri Lanka 2024, this year\u2019s event promises to be even more impactful, bringing together voices that matter to spark dialogue and drive meaningful change.\n\nCentered around the theme \u201cBeyond the Surface: Rethinking the Realities of Being a Woman,\u201d SHEvolve \u201926 aims to challenge societal norms, address stigmas, and foster a deeper understanding of issues surrounding women\u2019s lives. The event will feature a compelling panel discussion with distinguished panelists, including Ms. Gangulee Walpola, the Chief Guest of the event and an Attorney-at-Law based in Sri Lanka. She holds a Master\u2019s degree in Law from the University of West London and currently works as a corporate attorney at a large manufacturing company. Alongside her legal work, she is also a professional singer and a content creator, Ms. Sade Greenwood, the Miss World Sri Lanka 2021 and the Co-founder of Mullwood, Sri Lanka\u2019s first hair care brand for curly hair. She is also an advocate for self-expression and confidence, using her platform to promote inclusivity, beauty diversity, and women\u2019s empowerment, Dr. Ayisha Ziauddin, a Family Medicine Physician, the current secretary of Zonta One Club of Colombo and the co-founder of the Muslim Women\u2019s Collective, and Ms. Vithara Mannage, a lecturer at APIIT Sri Lanka specializing in Entrepreneurship and Business Management, with an MBA (Distinction) from the University of Staffordshire and current PhD candidate at the University of Colombo. Each panelist will bring unique perspectives to critical topics:"
