    "md5": "696948cac29fbd3d8a4bd6ee117aed7a",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1919,
    "chunk_text": "You do not need a university degree to verify this. You only need a calendar and the courage to look. Yet the government \u2014 a government that has shown again and again its contempt for the five precepts (sila), its addiction to corruption, and its cunning manipulation of everything sacred \u2014 now dares to alter the birth certificate of the Buddha himself.\n\nIf this is true, it is not a policy change. It is a spiritual crime. I struggle to find adequate words for its seriousness.\n\nI am not exaggerating. I am observing. Once respect for the sacred dies, everything becomes negotiable. And when everything is negotiable, nothing is true.\n\nWhere is our wisdom? A hard question for monks and lay people\n\nI practice the Buddha\u2019s path every day. I develop kindness (metta) and compassion (karuna) even toward those who insult me. I refuse to let a single word of hatred leave my lips. But I will not betray the truth.\n\nSo let me ask, without anger but with deep sorrow: How much real morality, concentration, and wisdom do most of today\u2019s monks and laypeople actually possess? How much general knowledge? How much education that goes beyond memorization?\n\nI travel across this country. I see brilliant minds wasted on partisan loyalty. I see temples filled with ritual but empty of reflection. I see a society that has forgotten how to calculate a Poya date, let alone meditate on anicca (impermanence). The lethargy and despair are not accidents. They are harvests. We planted carelessness. We are reaping foolishness.\n\nLet me say something uncomfortable. A democracy only works when voters are intelligent enough to choose leaders of character. Sri Lanka has proven, year after year, that we are not there yet. Without hatred, without malice, I state the obvious: we have given birth to a state that is extremely low and despicable. Not because of one man or one party, but because millions of us refused to think."
  },
